{
  "name": "sms-stop-handler",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Opt-outs.** A reply of STOP (any case; also STOPALL, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, QUIT) puts the number on the `sms_optout` Data Table and sends one confirmation. review-booster and missed-call-text-back both check that table before any text goes out. Point your SMS provider's \"incoming message\" webhook here.\n\n**Swapping the stand-in for a real SMS service (Twilio, ClickSend, MessageMedia):** in the \"Config\" node change `sms_api_url` to the provider's send-message URL, then on each \"Send ...\" HTTP Request node attach that provider's credential (an n8n credential you create, shown here as \"SMS provider (replace me)\") and adjust the JSON field names (`to`, `from`, `body`) to the provider's. The checks, duplicate handling and logging around it do not change.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "e5b4e35b-1428-9f60-8e76-090c6796c157",
      "position": [
        0,
        -330
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Inbound SMS",
